    {
      "object_id": "mathia_interpretation_b4de204a968a09a22920fcfeb649a8d6eee708e865d38d92ab1dd4cc97cd521b",
      "object_role": "interpretation",
      "proposed_content": "The construction bins M at multiplicative resolution 1+T^{-1}, keeps the minimum representative of each occupied bin in M', and defines r from enlarged, potentially overlapping neighborhoods of f(n)^2 mass. This compresses the support to |M'| ≤ |M| ≤ N while forgetting exact integer identity within a bin. It is not exact mass preservation: bounded overlap gives the one-sided norm bound in (19), with factor 3, and (21) one-sidedly lower-transfers selected exact relations mk=n in M to pairs in M' satisfying |km'/n'−1| ≤ 3/T. With N=⌊T^κ⌋ and the Gaussian, rapid Fourier decay and Cauchy–Schwarz then control off-diagonal contributions to the weighted L2 norm.",
