    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_8f0272fb3e79a815e1ca03e63191b36b6d792270c1da7369bc46ebd4f412622a",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Kernel parity coordinates the analytic projection with the sign structure available to resonance: the odd derivative-Gaussian has purely imaginary Fourier weights and routes the conditional S formula to a positive coefficient bound only after taking an imaginary component, yielding control of max |S|, whereas the even Gaussian has positive real Fourier weights and routes the S1 formula to a one-sided positive maximum.",
